==Trivia==
*The game's name makes a pun in Japanese: The real-world city of Kyōto is spelled 京都, while the word Kyoutou in the game's name is spelled 京刀; the second kanji means "sword", one of Kyoutou Project's main recurring motifs. Kyou also happened to be the name of one of the main characters - specifically the spirit dwelling within [[Kyosaka Nanaho (Legend Rare Cat)|Kyosaka Nanaho]]'s sword Honoka - so the title could literally mean Project of Kyou's Sword.

